  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/rev2500.html",
  "prefLabel": "Rev 2501.09 Electronic funds transfer (EFT)",
  "priorExpiration": "2005-11-27",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Rev 2501.09 “Electronic funds transfer (EFT)” means any transfer of funds, other than a transaction originated by check, draft, or similar paper instrument, which is initiated through an electronic terminal or computer to order, instruct, or authorize a financial institution to debit or credit an account.\n\nSource. #6639, eff 11-27-97, EXPIRED 11-27-05\n\nNew. #8495, eff 11-30-05 (formerly Rev 2501.07); ss by #10484, eff 12-5-13 (from Rev 2501.08); ss by #12907, eff 10-23-19; ss by #13724, eff 8-18-23 (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Rev 2500)",
